WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — interface-economics (90s) Narrator Lily

1
00:00:01.673 --> 00:00:05.050
In Ariane 501 and Mars Climate Orbiter,

2
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:12.843
individual modules behaved exactly as coded while unwritten interface contracts shattered.

3
00:00:17.136 --> 00:00:18.894
Under deadline pressure,

4
00:00:18.894 --> 00:00:27.247
documenting and proving boundary invariants penalizes the upstream schedule while downstream teams reap stability.

5
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:41.313
This three-dimensional gate illustrates untyped cross-team payloads compressed through explicit unit, range, and totality contracts.

6
00:00:45.606 --> 00:00:51.378
Side-by-side visual ledgers classify every published figure honestly,

7
00:00:51.378 --> 00:00:55.560
refusing to add apples, models, and opinion polls.

8
00:00:59.853 --> 00:01:09.271
Across aerospace, finance, and enterprise stacks, boundary reconciliation consumes a massive share of engineering budgets.

9
00:01:13.564 --> 00:01:21.750
Lowering verification cost via total Forms and static manifest checks solves the public-good bottleneck directly.
